    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nAn empty contiguous slice currently accesses `sequence_pointers[start]`; at or beyond the dataset end that pointer does not exist. Return the correctly shaped empty result before reading data. Multimodal results retain their empty mode array and noncontiguous slices remain rejected.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted draft. Human author review and NVIDIA GPU/CI validation are pending.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a narrowly scoped reproduced bug fix.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe six real builder/write/read cases all failed before the patch and pass after it. They cover normal and multimodal datasets, both file and mmap readers for populated datasets, a valid empty file-reader dataset, end/out-of-range/reversed/zero-width slices, and unchanged normal reads/noncontiguous rejection.\n\n- Focused CPU validation: **6 passed** using actual production imports and generated fixtures; no production modules or functions are replaced by stubs.\n- Command: `/opt/cpu-review/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/data tests/unit_tests/data/test_empty_dataset_slice.py -q`.\n- CPU environment: Linux container, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.8 CPU, real Triton package for imports. `--confcutdir` excludes the parent suite's unrelated GPU/data fixtures; this is not the canonical NVIDIA development image or full distributed test run.\n- Repository `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully: Black, isort, Pylint and Ruff blocking checks passed.\n- The formatter's informational mypy step reports 27 indexed_dataset diagnostics. The same 27 diagnostic messages are present in baseline; its configured blocking checks pass.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the repository autoformatter\n\nNo GPU kernel is added or modified.\n",
